---
description: Bash style for devmagic's scripts, install.sh and get.sh
globs: ["*.sh", "includes/**", "tools/**", "utilities/**", "build/**"]
---

# Shell scripts

- `#!/usr/bin/env bash` and `set -euo pipefail` (or `set -Eeuo pipefail` with
  a trap) in entry points. Files in `includes/`, `tools/` and `utilities/` only
  define functions; `mklocalenv.sh` sources them from `script_dir`.
- Log with the `devmagic_log_*` functions from `utilities/colors-logging.sh`
  in the command itself; `install.sh` and `get.sh` keep their own small
  loggers, since they run before anything is installed.
- Quote every expansion. Use arrays for argument lists. No `eval`. Never build
  a command from user input as a string.
- `sudo` only for the step that needs it, never for the whole script.
  `install.sh` refuses to run as root.
- Replace files atomically: write a temp file in the same folder, then `mv`.
- Downloads are checked before use: `get.sh` verifies the `.sha256` with
  `sha256sum -c` before it unpacks anything, and works in a `mktemp -d`
  folder it removes on exit.
- Interactive questions read from the terminal, so `curl ... | bash` still
  works: `get.sh` runs `install.sh` with `< /dev/tty` when there is one.
- Under `set -e`, a final `cond && cmd` returns 1 when `cond` is false; use
  `if` for anything that is not the last word.
- `shellcheck -x` passes with no warnings for new and changed scripts.
